  "problem": "What is missing in the following sentence?\n\nA drink contains $9$ fluid ounces of pure lemon juice and $13$ fluid ounces of clean water, so there are $\\boxed{}$ fluid ounces of pure lemon juice for each fluid ounce of distilled water.",
  "worked_solution": "The ratio of the fluid ounces of pure lemon juice to the fluid ounces of clean water is  $9:13.$ \n\nWe can rewrite this ratio as a fraction, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\frac{9}{13}\n$$\n\nThis means that there are $\\frac{9}{13}$ fluid ounces of pure lemon juice for each fluid ounce of clean water.",
